---
title: Green Curry Chicken
course: main
cuisine: thai
servings: 5
time_active: 25
time_total: 40
leftovers: great
tags: [weeknight, one-pot]
description: Chicken thighs simmered in coconut green curry with spinach, bell pepper, and lime.
---

Cook @jasmine rice{2%cups} as usual.

Cut @chicken thighs{2%lb}(boneless, skinless) into 1½-inch chunks and toss with @salt{1%tsp}. Open @coconut milk{2%cans}(13.5 oz full-fat, unshaken) and spoon off about ½ cup of the thick cream from the top of one can.

Heat @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium-high. Brown the chicken in a single layer, turning once, ~{5-6%minutes}; it needn't cook through. Move to a plate.

Lower the heat to medium. Cook @yellow onion{1}(thinly sliced) until soft, ~{4%minutes}.

Add @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @green curry paste{3-4%tbsp}, the reserved coconut cream, and @?jalapeño{1}(sliced). Fry, stirring, until very fragrant and the oil separates, ~{2%minutes}.

Stir in the rest of the coconut milk, @chicken broth{1/2%cup}, @fish sauce{1%tbsp}, and @sugar{1%tsp}. Return the chicken and its juices and simmer gently, uncovered, ~{10%minutes}. Add @?red bell pepper{1}(sliced) and simmer until the chicken is cooked through and the pepper is crisp-tender, ~{5%minutes}.

Off the heat, stir in @baby spinach{8%oz} until wilted, then the juice of one of the @limes{2}. Taste and adjust with fish sauce, sugar, lime, or more paste.

Serve over the rice with @cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped, or Thai basil) and wedges of the other lime.

> Paste heat varies: start with 3 tbsp of Maesri or Mae Ploy; mild Thai Kitchen may need the whole jar.

> With only one can of coconut milk: fry the paste in oil instead of cream, use 2–3 tbsp paste and 1 cup broth, and stir in ¼ cup heavy cream at the end.
